@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}
<div class="prose">
<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<p class="text-muted">Last updated: 2 October 2026</p>

<p>
    DonationTracker is a practice project, not a live service. It runs on the
    computer of whoever starts it. Please do not enter real personal data.
</p>

<h2 class="mt-4">What the app stores</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Supporters: full name, email address and the date the record was created.</li>
    <li>Donations: the supporter, the amount and the date of the donation.</li>
    <li>Staff accounts: the email address used to sign in and a hashed password. The password itself is never stored.</li>
</ul>
<p>
    The sample records added by the seed script are made up and do not describe
    real people.
</p>

<h2 class="mt-4">Where it is stored</h2>
<p>
    Everything is saved in a SQL Server LocalDB database on the machine running
    the app. Nothing is sent to any other server, service or third party.
</p>

<h2 class="mt-4">Cookies</h2>
<p>
    The app sets two cookies, both needed for it to work: an anti-forgery cookie
    that protects the forms from cross-site request forgery, and a sign-in
    cookie that keeps a member of staff signed in until they sign out or close
    the browser. There are no analytics, advertising or tracking cookies.
</p>

<h2 class="mt-4">Third parties</h2>
<p>
    None. Bootstrap and jQuery are served from the app itself, so viewing a page
    makes no requests to outside sites.
</p>

<h2 class="mt-4">Keeping and removing data</h2>
<p>
    Records stay in the local database until that database is deleted. The app
    has no delete pages; a record can be changed on its edit page.
</p>

<h2 class="mt-4">Questions</h2>
<p>
    Please raise an issue on the
    <a href="https://github.com/AJWCTech/donation-tracker-aspnet-mvc">project's GitHub repository</a>.
</p>
</div>
